      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5,000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. The usual maximum for a healthy adult is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5 g dose is already above the normal single-dose limit of 1 g. At 15 g/day, this patient would be at serious risk of acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some common regimens are:\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also check the intended dose with your resident or attending before it goes in."
      }
